eme of this  story and i think it's worth repeating  here you followed your conscience in  hopes that others would follow theirs  you didn't do it for a reward or a pat  on the head the universe never tells us  if we did right or wrong it's more  important to try to help people and to  know that you did more important that  someone else's life gets better than for  you to feel good about yourself you  never know the effect you might have on  someone not really maybe one cruel thing  you said haunts them forever maybe one  moment of kindness gives them comfort or  courage maybe you said the one thing  they needed to hear it doesn't matter if  you ever know you just have to try as  she's talking you see that during  marco's speech on the pella philip left  his post and boarded the repair skiff he  left before they started burning for the  ring and survived to start a new life  away from his father you see him doing  that as he enters his name as philip  nagata after her words holden starts to  talk about what they might do for work  now that the war is over and mentions  how the protomolecule sample is still  missing and naomi smiles and tells him  let's just stay here for a minute it  cuts to an exterior shot of the rossi  and you watch it as it moves into the  distance until you can no longer see it  and the series ends there in the closing  credits scene you can make out the  orbital platforms behind the names and  start to see hints of the red that's  there when ships disappear after the  energy threshold was met a hint that  something ominous awaits if the rest of  the series is ever adapted the end of a  beloved tv series is always a  bittersweet occasion and in the case of  the expanse a little more so considering  we know there's more to the story season  six had some external forces that made  things difficult here and i think that  all things considered they delivered an  ending that does the story and the  characters justice if holden has a  superpower it's that he can still see  the good in humans even when faced with  overwhelming evidence to the contrary at  its core the idea of trying to make the  world a better place in your small  corner of the solar system and following  your conscience with no expectation of a  reward in hopes that others might do the  same comes out again and again and even  though the politics are complicated and  a purely happy ending feels like it  would be pretty fragile having drummer  end up as the trade union president is a  satisfying conclusion the show switched  some things up and holden accepting the  job just to resign and i like the added  dimension of them outplaying avasarala  as the way to make that happen marco  relearned the lesson that the inners  will never see belters as equals the  hard way and becoming duarte's useful  idiot and i always thought of philip's  ending as being the product of being  born into an impossible situation he's  given a chance to maybe make up for his  crimes but he has to do it himself if  you think about it he can't really even  try to reunite with his mother  considering the circumstances she has to  mourn his death in a situation where she  chose the family she found and there's a  nice line from just before what i read  at the beginning that sums this up i  will carry this guilt and sadness for  the rest of my life was just as true as  i lost my son years ago her comfort was  that she was still alive that jim was  and amos and alex bobby and clarissa  there's the idea that both of these  things can exist together without  necessarily canceling each other out and  i think that ties into what we heard at  the beginning of all the x-ray features  this season in the doctrine of one ship  there's just one hole with countless  parts working together like the cells of  a single organism there are factions and  tribes in different political interests  inequalities built into the system and  exploitation that creates conditions  where people like marco can emerge and  if you throw in something like the proto  molecule and the opening of the ringgate  network that connects to all these new  systems with resources free for the  taking that's the impetus for conflict  on the civilizational scale i think the  message is a hopeful one rooted in  realistic relatable characters that also  happen to fly around in spaceships the  political tensions make sense and bring  out the best and the worst of humanity  in the end the wars are over and the  belters have a brighter future and  fighting for the people you care about  still matters i'm sad the expanse is  over but glad i got to experience it and  i think that's a good place to leave  things let me know what you thought  about the finale in the final season and  the series as a whole in the comments  there were a lot of famous sci-fi  characters that made the ultimate  sacrifice in that assault on the ring  station there's so much great character  stuff in the finale and will be diving a  lot deeper into that in the live stream  which i'll put a link to in the pinned  comment if you feel unsatisfied with  where the proto-molecule storyline was  left i highly recommend reading the  books to see what happens with that the  ending is also very satisfying i have a  couple of other videos planned to put  out over the next week so make sure you  check back for those please like this  video if you enjoyed it please subscribe  to my channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon
 

